  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Departure Board",
    "overview": "The console reads like a station departure board. Railway navy owns the frame: the top bar and the action board, where a large signal-yellow count says how many things wait for the operator and timetable rows say what each one is. Everything below the board is a cool light working ground with white panels, set dense and quiet, so that the board stays the loudest thing on any screen.\n\nHierarchy comes from scale contrast and colour discipline, not from decoration. Times, user IDs and money are set in a condensed face with tabular figures so columns align like a printed timetable; Chinese text runs in the system 黑体 stack. One rule weight, three ink values, 2px corners, and no decorative shadow keep the surface flat and legible. Colour is semantic before it is atmospheric: yellow means \"your hand is needed\", red means unknown or critical, green means running or settled, amber means below threshold or stale.\n\nThe system rejects the category default of a KPI-card row over tabs and grey tables. A dashboard tile grid is the thing this board replaces.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Navy frame (shell, action board, login gate) over a cool light ground with white panels.",
      "Signal yellow reserved for things awaiting the operator.",
      "Tabular condensed figures for every time, ID and amount.",
      "One 1px rule weight, 2px corners, flat surfaces.",
      "Dense, desktop-first tables that restack into cards on phones."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Operator's Hand Rule",
        "body": "Signal yellow appears only on things awaiting the operator: pending counts, approve actions, the tally number. Never use it for decoration, branding, or general emphasis.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Variant Rule",
        "body": "Every state colour has a dark text value tuned for WCAG AA on its own tint (ok, danger, caution) and a brighter value for fills and navy (ok-on-navy, danger-fill / danger-on-navy, caution-fill / caution-on-navy). Text on a light tint always takes the dark value.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Uncertainty Is Red Rule",
        "body": "Unknown and blocked are alarm red, never caution amber and never neutral grey; uncertainty must look different from success and from failure.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Figures Rule",
        "body": "Every time, user ID and amount takes the figures face with `tnum` and `lnum` on. A face that ships no true tabular figures is not eligible, however well it fits otherwise (Barlow Semi Condensed was rejected for this).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Scale Contrast Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy is carried by size jumps between figures and labels (112 / 52 / 26 against 12-14), not by colour fills, cards, or extra weights.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Board Rule",
        "body": "Panels, the board, strips and buttons never cast shadows. Shadow means \"this floats above the page right now\", and only toasts and modal dialogs float.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep signal yellow for things waiting on the operator: tab counts, approve buttons, the tally, the 待审批 state.",
      "Do set every time, ID and amount in Fira Sans Condensed with `tnum` and `lnum` on, and right-align money columns.",
      "Do use the dark text values (ok #18744a, danger #c22f35, caution #855800) on their tints, and the brighter variants only for fills and on navy.",
      "Do use one 1px rule weight and the single 2px corner on every container, button, badge and input.",
      "Do show unknown and blocked in alarm red, and missing data as a dashed or muted state, never as success.",
      "Do restack wide tables into labelled cards below 640px rather than shrinking text.",
      "Do keep motion short and functional (0.15s state transitions on the ease-out curve), and honour reduced motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't build a KPI-card row over tabs and grey tables; the action board is the summary.",
      "Don't use signal yellow for decoration, branding, highlights or general warnings.",
      "Don't add decorative shadows to panels, the board, strips or buttons; only toasts and modal dialogs float.",
      "Don't round corners past 2px or introduce pill and circular shapes.",
      "Don't use a figures face without true tabular figures.",
      "Don't expand more than one board row at a time."
    ]
  }
